# Committed, NON-SECRET production defaults. Next.js loads this file for
# `next build` / `next start`; anything already present in the real process
# environment (a Vercel dashboard variable) wins over it, so this is a floor,
# never an override.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: lib/adsense.ts throws on a missing or malformed
# publisher id in a production build. That assertion is the point — it makes a
# wrong id impossible to ship — but it would also fail the very first deploy of
# this branch if the Vercel variable hadn't been added yet. The id is public
# (it is emitted in the page HTML on every request), so committing it as a
# build-time default costs nothing and removes that failure mode.
#
# Set the same variable in the Vercel project (Production + Preview) as the
# real source of truth; this file only guarantees the build can never be
# bricked by its absence. Nothing secret may ever be added here.

NEXT_PUBLIC_ADSENSE_CLIENT_ID="ca-pub-6842128782879909"
